# SESSION 5: UML USE CASE MODELING

**Project Title:** Cybersecurity Awareness Platform for Phishing Detection and Prevention

**Domain:** Cybersecurity and Information Security

**Prepared By:** Ramjee Chaurasiya

**Role:** Team Leader

## 1. Aim

To identify the use cases of the Cybersecurity Awareness Platform for Phishing Detection and Prevention, create a UML Use Case Diagram, and prepare detailed use case descriptions to represent the functional requirements of the proposed system.

## 2. Objectives

- Identify the actors interacting with the proposed system.
- Identify and classify the major use cases.
- Create a UML Use Case Diagram using Draw.io or StarUML.
- Define the interactions between actors and system functions.
- Prepare use case description templates and narratives.
- Map the identified use cases to the requirements of the proposed software system.

## 3. Introduction

UML (Unified Modeling Language) is a standard modeling language used to visualize, specify, and document software systems. Use Case Modeling is a UML technique that represents the functional requirements of a system from the perspective of its users.

A Use Case Diagram identifies the actors, use cases, and system boundary. Actors represent external entities that interact with the system, while use cases represent the services or functions provided by the system.

The proposed Cybersecurity Awareness Platform for Phishing Detection and Prevention aims to improve users' cybersecurity awareness through educational training, phishing simulations, quizzes, performance assessment, and feedback.

Use Case Modeling helps define how users interact with the platform and provides a clear foundation for subsequent software design, development, and testing.

## 4. Use Case Identification

### 4.1 Actors

**Actor 1: End User**

The End User is the primary actor who uses the platform to improve cybersecurity awareness.

Responsibilities:
- Register and log in.
- Access cybersecurity training.
- Learn about phishing attacks.
- Participate in safe phishing simulations.
- Attempt cybersecurity quizzes.
- View results and learning progress.
- Receive performance feedback.

**Actor 2: Administrator**

The Administrator manages the educational content and quiz information of the platform.

Responsibilities:
- Log in using authorized credentials.
- Add or update cybersecurity training material.
- Manage quiz questions.
- Maintain relevant educational content.

### 4.2 Identified Use Cases

| Use Case ID | Use Case Name | Primary Actor |
|---|---|---|
| UC-01 | Register Account | End User |
| UC-02 | Log In | End User, Administrator |
| UC-03 | Access Cybersecurity Training | End User |
| UC-04 | Learn About Phishing | End User |
| UC-05 | Participate in Phishing Simulation | End User |
| UC-06 | Attempt Cybersecurity Quiz | End User |
| UC-07 | View Results and Progress | End User |
| UC-08 | Receive Performance Feedback | End User |
| UC-09 | Manage Training Content | Administrator |
| UC-10 | Manage Quiz Questions | Administrator |

These use cases represent the proposed functional scope of the platform and should be verified against the actual application before being treated as implemented functionality.

